{"content":"Root cause found and fixed: in sqlparse/filters/reindent.py, ReindentFilter._next_token had an inverted condition (`if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN')`) that caused it to recurse into itself with `idx=None` whenever the token found was NOT 'BETWEEN' (the common case), rather than only when it WAS 'BETWEEN' (the intended BETWEEN...AND skip logic). This led to `tlist.token_next_by(idx=None)` doing `idx += 1` on None, raising `TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: 'NoneType' and 'int'`. This broke sqlparse.format(..., reindent=True) entirely, cascading into 41 failing checks (CLI formatting, reindent-based tests, etc.).

Fix: corrected the condition to `if token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN':` so recursion only happens to skip past the AND in a BETWEEN...AND pair, and otherwise the found split-keyword token is returned immediately as intended.

Verified via `check`: 41 passing, 0 failing.","tool_calls":[{"id":"final_1","name":"finish","arguments":{"summary":"Fixed regression in sqlparse/filters/reindent.py: ReindentFilter._next_token had an inverted condition causing infinite/erroneous recursion with idx=None, triggering 'TypeError: unsupported operand type(s) for +=: NoneType and int' whenever reindent formatting encountered any split keyword that wasn't 'BETWEEN'. Changed `if not (token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN'):` to `if token and token.normalized == 'BETWEEN':` so the BETWEEN...AND skip logic only triggers for actual BETWEEN tokens, and other split keywords are returned directly. This restores correct behavior for sqlparse.format(reindent=True) and all downstream CLI/formatting functionality. Confirmed via check tool: 41/41 previously failing hidden tests now pass, 0 failing."}}]}
